Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> Patashu schrieb:
>> On Apr 9, 10:51 am, purple arcanist <ejg_...@yahoo.com> wrote:
>>> Some things that could be wise wishes in real life:
>>> [...]
>> I recall reading at one point an in-depth list of what kinds of wishes
>> would be useful in real life. I think it was in rgrn?
>>
>> [...] would be great, but how do you stop it being stolen from you?
> 
> That's an issue with quite all objects, magical or otherwise overly
> useful. So in RL I probably abstain from wishing for objects that I
> have to carefully keep with me to be useful.

Yup. So here's my list, with that caveat in mind.

Blessed PYEC. I could reclaim that drawer that is full of wall warts for
all of my rechargeable gadgets. Would it work on a plug-in hybrid or
full electric car? It stays in the fire safe with all of the other
credit cards that I only use once a year to keep the account active.

Could I replace the lenses in my glasses with The Eyes of the Overworld?
Who needs a GPS map, then? And who steals someone's glasses?

A horn of plenty, especially combined with the blessed PYEC. The deep
freezer in the basement is suddenly much less needed. Leave it on the
coffee table with some wax fruit in the opening and it looks like any
other decorative cornucopia.

A blessed tin of green dragon meat for immediate consumption. Especially
if allergies can be counted as a poison effect.

A ring of adornment for meetings and job interviews. Stays in the
jewelry box otherwise.

A fireproof alchemy smock #named "KISS THE COOK" and fireproof leather
gloves for grilling season. Or gauntlets of dexterity if you want to
pull flashy knife tricks for the crowd. :)

For pure mundane utility, a blessed tin opener. Because it always opens
the tin in one turn, which is more than I can say about any RL tin
opener I've ever owned...

> From a practical POV any bag would be nice, because I could stuff
> in all the items that require so much store room. :-)  A plain old
> sack, or maybe oilskin, is probably better than a bag holding which
> might, because of its magic power, be more likely target of theft.

Oilskin definitely. Especially for loose definitions of "sack" and it
can come in the form of a messenger bag or laptop bag.


